ater sources or build  infrastructure of their own one  potential provider canadian-based  utility epcor has said it's willing to  help but it'll need at least two years  to get up and running Porter called the  situation A cautionary tale even though  there won't be a lot of new algorithms  it is a signal that cities are paying  more attention to how they take care of  the water supplies that they have in  there a sentiment echoed by Scottsdale  mayor David Ortega who spoke with Brook  silver Braga for CBS Saturday morning  last November why not just let those few  people keep the water for a little  longer they should manage their own  destiny with their own water yeah we  have to adapt and then we have to adapt  more and we have to adapt more for CBS  mornings I'm Chris Van Cleave
 

